&lt;p&gt;I’m an assistant professor of international politics and policy at Georgetown University in Qatar. I research nonprofits and NGOs, human rights, public policy/administration, and causal inference.&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I teach classes about R, data science, data visualization, and causal inference (as well as non-technical classes on economics nonprofits, and public administration). &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.andrewheiss.com/teaching/&quot;&gt;All my course materials&lt;/a&gt; are open source, Creative Commons-licensed, and free!&lt;/p&gt; 
&lt;p&gt;I’m also a &lt;a href=&quot;https://education.rstudio.com/trainers/people/heiss+andrew/&quot;&gt;certified RStudio instructor&lt;/a&gt; and a &lt;a href=&quot;https://posit.co/products/enterprise/academy/&quot;&gt;Posit Academy mentor&lt;/a&gt; and absolutely love teaching how to use R and the tidyverse.&lt;/p&gt; 
